========================================================================
5. Keeping the dictionaries: aggregate() over collect_list()
========================================================================
aggregate(collect_list(tally), {}, add_tallies) same answer? True
It works, but collect_list() gathers EVERY tally of a county in one
place (that's groupByKey(), not foldByKey()): every tally crosses the
network and no votes are added before the shuffle. To aggregate
dictionaries, explode() them into rows first.

========================================================================
6. A common mistake: NULL is not zero
========================================================================
+-----------+----+-----+------+--------+-----+
|     county| Lee|Patel|Rivera|write-in|total|
+-----------+----+-----+------+--------+-----+
|    Alameda|1210| 1200|   510|       7| 2927|
|  San Mateo| 540|  710|   155|    NULL| NULL|
|Santa Clara|1235| 1385|   348|       4| 2972|
+-----------+----+-----+------+--------+-----+

San Mateo's total is NULL: in SQL, anything + NULL is NULL. One NULL
(no write-in votes) erased 1,405 real votes.

With fillna(0) first:
+-----------+----+-----+------+--------+-----+
|     county| Lee|Patel|Rivera|write-in|total|
+-----------+----+-----+------+--------+-----+
|    Alameda|1210| 1200|   510|       7| 2927|
|  San Mateo| 540|  710|   155|       0| 1405|
|Santa Clara|1235| 1385|   348|       4| 2972|
+-----------+----+-----+------+--------+-----+

The totals now match the rollup() in section 4.
